  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 42 Chapter 698\n \n      MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 9493-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the banking law and the executive law, in relation\n        to certain notices and services upon application for a  mortgage\n        guaranteed  under  the  \"Servicemen's Readjustment Act of 1944\";\n        and providing for the repeal of certain provisions upon  expira-\n        tion thereof\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would ensure that veterans are provided the opportunity to\nreceive free counseling to protect their  financial  interests  as  they\nseek  to  achieve  home  ownership.  This  is a worthy goal that I fully\nsupport.\n \n  However, there are certain technical issues with the bill as currently\ndrafted that would prevent the bill from  achieving  its  stated  objec-\ntives.  I have reached agreement with the Legislature to limit potential\nconflicts of interest involving the counselors providing financial guid-\nance  to  veterans  by requiring that the counselors be certified by the\nUnited States Department of  Housing  and  Urban  Development,  and,  by\ngranting  State agencies the authority to promulgate further regulations\nas needed. This will  ensure  that  the  loan  counseling  and  guidance\nprovided to veterans is in their best financial interest.\n \n  Based on this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2022
 },
